edits.new:
- the 19 logins of the same 19 names, one per schema, each owning its own schema and holding no grant, no USAGE and no object privilege on any other `rwb_*` schema (Arch v5 slide 29: "each service has one database login that owns its schema and has no grant on any other schema");
- schema creation (GAP-1384): each schema is owned by its own login, UTF8 with the server default collation, the default tablespace, ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES granted to the owning login only, search_path set to the service's own schema, and all 19 schemas created once by the ACE DBA account in one transaction;
- environments (GAP-1385): DEV and SIT receive the 19 schemas and logins in wave 0 by this story; UAT and PROD receive them by the same idempotent script at the release of the first service of each wave; the ACE DBA role runs the script and each run carries its own change record;
- failover test (GAP-2066): the ACE database failover test is owned by this story with the ACE DBA; the restore test of documents and the database is owned by P5 rwb-document with RWB-PLT-DB;
- login names (GAP-0688, GAP-0758, GAP-1037): the rwb-case and rwb-document login names stay the DP-02 placeholders until the ACE DB team names them with their grants and secret references, which are Not specified in the source documents (GAP-1037);
